/* Hinglish: p14 (coding-book rewrite and playbook tracks). Keyed on the exact English line. */
Object.assign(window.HING = window.HING || {}, {

  'Build or buy: comparing a vendor with your own build':
    'Build ya buy: vendor ko apne build se compare karna',
  'Build-or-buy decisions often turn on price and demo quality, which matter less than they seem. You will test a vendor with your own answer key, cost both options over two years, and write down in advance what would change your decision.':
    'Build-or-buy faisle aksar price aur demo quality par ghoomte hain, jo dikhne se kam maayne rakhte hain. Aap apni answer key se vendor ko test karenge, do saal tak dono vikalpon ki cost nikaalenge, aur pehle se likhenge ki aapka faisla kya badlega.',
  'Run the same evaluation on a vendor and on your own build, and compare like with like.':
    'Vendor aur apne build par ek hi evaluation chalaana, aur barabar ki tulna karna.',
  'Write down what would make you change the decision later, before you make it.':
    'Faisla lene se pehle likhna ki baad mein use kya badlega.',
  'A build-or-buy recommendation with a review date':
    'Review date ke saath build-or-buy recommendation',
  'Make a real build-or-buy recommendation using evidence you gathered, including the conditions under which it stops being right.':
    'Apne ikattha kiye saboot se asli build-or-buy recommendation dijiye, un sharton samet jinme woh sahi nahi rehti.',
  'State the capability in one line, and whether it is core or supporting for your product.':
    'Kshamata ek line mein bataiye, aur kya yeh aapke product ke liye core hai ya sahaayak.',
  'Run your answer key against at least one vendor trial, and record its results next to your own build’s.':
    'Kam se kam ek vendor trial par apni answer key chalaiye, aur uske results apne build ke results ke bagal mein record kijiye.',
  'Cost both over two years, including evaluation, maintenance and incident handling.':
    'Dono ki do saal ki cost nikaaliye, evaluation, maintenance aur incidents sambhaalne samet.',
  'Add the time until each reaches users. Say which matters more here and why.':
    'Har ek ke users tak pahunchne ka samay jodiye. Bataiye yahan kya zyada maayne rakhta hai aur kyun.',
  'For the buy option, write what you would need in order to leave, and how long it would take.':
    'Buy vikalp ke liye likhiye ki chhodne ke liye kya chahiye, aur kitna samay lagega.',
  'Write the two triggers that would reverse the decision, and the date you will review them.':
    'Woh do triggers likhiye jo faisla palat denge, aur woh date jab aap unka review karenge.',
  'You measured both options against the same answer key.':
    'Aapne dono vikalpon ko ek hi answer key se naapa.',
  'The build cost includes maintenance and evaluation, not just tokens.':
    'Build cost mein maintenance aur evaluation hai, sirf tokens nahi.',
  'The recommendation names what would make it wrong, with a review date.':
    'Recommendation review date ke saath batati hai ki use galat kya karega.',
  'A spec describes a measured range':
    'Spec ek naapi hui range describe karta hai',
  'So you can define “good enough” before you compare options.':
    'Taaki vikalpon ki tulna se pehle aap “kaafi achha” ki paribhasha de sakein.',
  'So you can test a vendor instead of trusting a demo.':
    'Taaki aap demo par bharosa karne ki jagah vendor ko test kar sakein.',
  'No new setup. Bring the acceptance criteria from Chapter 18 and the answer key from Chapter 6.':
    'Koi naya setup nahi. Chapter 18 ke acceptance criteria aur Chapter 6 ki answer key le aaiye.',
  'At some point someone will propose buying a product that does what you have learned to build. The discussion usually focuses on price and the demo. Neither decides the question.':
    'Kabhi na kabhi koi aisa product khareedne ka prastaav dega jo woh karta hai jo aapne banaana seekha. Baatcheet aam taur par price aur demo par tikti hai. Dono mein se koi sawaal tay nahi karta.',
  'You are rarely buying the model; most vendors use the same models. You are buying the connectors, the permissions, the audit trail, the support contract, and someone else handling incidents.':
    'Aap shayad hi model khareed rahe hote hain; zyadatar vendors wahi models use karte hain. Aap connectors, permissions, audit trail, support contract, aur incidents sambhaalne wala koi aur khareed rahe hote hain.',
  'Test the vendor with your answer key':
    'Apni answer key se vendor ko test kijiye',
  'Run your answer key against the vendor':
    'Vendor par apni answer key chalaiye',
  'Ask for a trial. Run your ten real questions through it and grade the answers against your key. Use your questions, not the vendor’s demo questions.':
    'Trial maangiye. Apne das asli sawaal usme chalaiye aur jawabon ko apni key se grade kijiye. Apne sawaal use kijiye, vendor ke demo sawaal nahi.',
  'The result is usually worse than the demo suggested and better than you feared. The unanswerable question and the second-language question usually show the biggest gap, because vendors rarely optimise for them.':
    'Result aam taur par demo ke hisaab se bura aur aapke darr se achha hota hai. Jawab na hone wala sawaal aur doosri bhasha wala sawaal aam taur par sabse bada gap dikhate hain, kyunki vendors shayad hi unke liye optimise karte hain.',
  'You are the only person in the negotiation who can run this test, because you have the answer key.':
    'Negotiation mein aap akele insaan hain jo yeh test chala sakte hain, kyunki answer key aapke paas hai.',
  'The questions that decide it':
    'Faisla karne wale sawaal',
  'Why it matters':
    'Yeh kyun maayne rakhta hai',
  'If your product exists to do this, you need to own it. If it is supporting plumbing, buying is usually right.':
    'Agar aapka product yahi karne ke liye hai, to aapko iska maalik hona chahiye. Agar yeh sahaayak plumbing hai, to khareedna aam taur par sahi hai.',
  'How often will it need to change?':
    'Ise kitni baar badalna padega?',
  'Something you tune weekly against your own data is hard to buy. Something stable is expensive to build.':
    'Jise aap har hafte apne data par tune karte hain use khareedna mushkil hai. Jo sthir hai use banaana mehnga hai.',
  'Who handles incidents at 2am?':
    'Raat 2 baje incidents kaun sambhaalta hai?',
  'A real cost that is often left out, and often larger than the licence.':
    'Ek asli cost jo aksar chhoot jaati hai, aur aksar licence se badi hoti hai.',
  'What happens if the vendor is acquired or shuts down?':
    'Agar vendor khareeda jaaye ya band ho jaaye to kya hoga?',
  'Ask what you would need in order to leave, and how long it would take. If nobody can answer, treat that as a risk.':
    'Poochhiye ki chhodne ke liye aapko kya chahiye, aur kitna samay lagega. Agar koi jawab na de sake, to ise risk maaniye.',
  'Cost both options over two years':
    'Do saal tak dono vikalpon ki cost nikaaliye',
  'Write the two-year cost of each option. For building, include the Chapter 15 costs plus what people usually leave out: evaluation, the person maintaining it, and rerunning the migration tests every time the underlying model changes.':
    'Har vikalp ki do saal ki cost likhiye. Banaane ke liye Chapter 15 ki costs aur woh jodiye jo log aam taur par chhodte hain: evaluation, ise sambhaalne wala insaan, aur har baar neeche ka model badalne par migration tests dobara chalaana.',
  'The build cost is usually two to four times the first estimate. The buy option often has a price increase at the next tier that nobody has read. Find both before you decide.':
    'Build cost aam taur par pehle andaaze ka do se chaar guna hoti hai. Buy vikalp mein aksar agle tier par price badhotri hoti hai jo kisi ne nahi padhi. Faisle se pehle dono dhoondhiye.',
  'Then add the time until each option reaches a user. A build that is cheaper over two years but arrives six months later can still be the wrong choice.':
    'Phir har vikalp ke user tak pahunchne ka samay jodiye. Do saal mein sasta lekin chhe mahine baad aane wala build phir bhi galat choice ho sakta hai.',
  'Decide what would change your mind':
    'Tay kijiye ki aapka mann kya badlega',
  'Write down what would make you change your mind, in both directions. What evidence would turn a build recommendation into a buy, and what would turn a buy into a build?':
    'Likhiye ki dono dishaon mein aapka mann kya badlega. Kaunsa saboot build recommendation ko buy mein badlega, aur kaunsa buy ko build mein?',
  'Writing this before deciding keeps the decision open to evidence. Common reasons to switch to buying: the maintenance falls on one person, or the capability turns out to be a commodity. Common reasons to switch to building: the vendor’s roadmap moves away from your needs, the price rises at the next tier, or the “plumbing” turns out to be why customers choose you. Put a date on when you will review it.':
    'Faisle se pehle yeh likhna faisle ko saboot ke liye khula rakhta hai. Buy ki taraf jaane ki aam wajahen: maintenance ek insaan par aa jaaye, ya kshamata aam cheez nikle. Build ki taraf jaane ki aam wajahen: vendor ka roadmap aapki zarooraton se door jaaye, agle tier par price badhe, ya “plumbing” hi woh nikle jiski wajah se customers aapko chunte hain. Review ki date tay kijiye.',
  'A common good answer is a mix: buy the plumbing and build the part that makes your product different. For example, use a vendor’s connectors and permissions, but own your retrieval and your evaluation.':
    'Ek aam achha jawab mela-jula hota hai: plumbing khareediye aur woh hissa banaiye jo aapke product ko alag banata hai. Jaise, vendor ke connectors aur permissions use kijiye, lekin retrieval aur evaluation apne rakhiye.',
  'Fine-tuning or not: choosing what to change':
    'Fine-tuning karein ya nahi: kya badalna hai chunna',
  'When a model is not good enough, you can change the instructions, the evidence, the training or the model. You will sort real failures into four kinds, match each kind to its fix, and cost a fine-tuning proposal honestly.':
    'Jab model kaafi achha nahi hota, to aap instructions, saboot, training ya model badal sakte hain. Aap asli failures ko chaar kismon mein baantenge, har kism ko uske fix se milaayenge, aur fine-tuning prastaav ki imaandaar cost nikaalenge.',
  'Name the four things you can change, and what each one actually fixes.':
    'Un chaar cheezon ka naam lena jinhe aap badal sakte hain, aur har ek asal mein kya theek karti hai.',
  'Say what must exist before the fine-tuning question can be answered.':
    'Batana ki fine-tuning ke sawaal ka jawab dene se pehle kya maujood hona chahiye.',
  'Answer a fine-tuning proposal with evidence':
    'Saboot ke saath fine-tuning prastaav ka jawab dijiye',
  'Someone will propose fine-tuning, and it will sound like the serious option. Find out which kinds of failure they actually have, and cost the proposal honestly, including the parts that are usually left off the slide.':
    'Koi fine-tuning ka prastaav dega, aur woh gambhir vikalp lagega. Pata lagaiye ki unke paas asal mein kis kism ke failures hain, aur prastaav ki imaandaar cost nikaaliye, un hisson samet jo aam taur par slide se chhoot jaate hain.',
  'Count them. The counts often settle the question before any technical discussion.':
    'Unhe giniye. Ginti aksar kisi technical charcha se pehle sawaal tay kar deti hai.',
  'For the largest group, name the cheapest change that would address it, and explain why it is cheaper.':
    'Sabse bade group ke liye sabse sasta badlaav bataiye jo use sambhaale, aur samjhaaiye ki woh sasta kyun hai.',
  'Cost the fine-tuning proposal properly: preparing data, training, evaluating, and repeating it every time the base model changes.':
    'Fine-tuning prastaav ki theek cost nikaaliye: data taiyaar karna, training, evaluation, aur har baar base model badalne par ise dohraana.',
  'Try a smaller or cheaper model with better retrieval, and measure whether quality actually drops.':
    'Behtar retrieval ke saath chhota ya sasta model try kijiye, aur naapiye ki quality sach mein girti hai ya nahi.',
  'Write a one-page recommendation, using the failure counts as the main argument.':
    'Failure counts ko main tark banaate hue ek page ki recommendation likhiye.',
  'You sorted real failures into the four kinds, with counts.':
    'Aapne asli failures ko ginti ke saath chaar kismon mein baanta.',
  'The cost of fine-tuning includes the recurring cost, not just the first run.':
    'Fine-tuning ki cost mein baar-baar ki cost hai, sirf pehla run nahi.',
  'You cannot choose a fix without knowing what is wrong and how often.':
    'Kya galat hai aur kitni baar, yeh jaane bina aap fix nahi chun sakte.',
  'Without one, you cannot see the effect of any change in this chapter.':
    'Iske bina aap is chapter ke kisi badlaav ka asar nahi dekh sakte.',
  'No notebook for this chapter. Open your failure taxonomy from Chapter 14.5, or collect ten real outputs from an AI feature you use every day.':
    'Is chapter ke liye koi notebook nahi. Chapter 14.5 ki apni failure taxonomy kholiye, ya roz use kiye kisi AI feature ke das asli outputs ikattha kijiye.',
  'At some point, usually in a roadmap review, someone will ask: <em>should we fine-tune?</em> It is usually asked before anyone has said what is wrong. Saying yes commits a quarter of work. Saying no can sound unambitious. The right answer starts with a diagnosis.':
    'Kabhi na kabhi, aam taur par roadmap review mein, koi poochhega: <em>kya hame fine-tune karna chahiye?</em> Aam taur par yeh kisi ke batane se pehle poochha jaata hai ki kya galat hai. Haan kehna ek quarter ka kaam tay karta hai. Na kehna mahatvakaanksha ki kami lag sakta hai. Sahi jawab diagnosis se shuru hota hai.',
  'Four things you can change':
    'Chaar cheezein jo aap badal sakte hain',
  'You can change <strong>the instructions</strong>, <strong>the evidence you give the model</strong>, <strong>the model’s training on your own examples</strong> (fine-tuning), or <strong>which model you use</strong>. Try them in that order.':
    'Aap <strong>instructions</strong>, <strong>model ko diya saboot</strong>, <strong>aapke examples par model ki training</strong> (fine-tuning), ya <strong>kaunsa model use karte hain</strong> badal sakte hain. Inhe isi kram mein try kijiye.',
  'Predict: your assistant confidently says the refund window is 30 days. The correct figure, published last month, is 45. Which of the four changes fixes it, and which will a meeting room usually suggest?':
    'Andaaza lagaiye: aapka assistant confident hokar kehta hai ki refund window 30 din hai. Pichhle mahine prakaashit sahi figure 45 hai. Chaar mein se kaunsa badlaav ise theek karta hai, aur meeting room aam taur par kya suggest karega?',
  'Better evidence. The system does not have the current policy, so it produces a plausible number from its training, as Chapter 2 described. A meeting will often suggest fine-tuning, because “teach the model our policies” sounds right. But a fine-tuned model needs retraining every time the number changes, and it still cannot show the user where 45 came from.':
    'Behtar saboot. System ke paas current policy nahi, isliye woh apni training se sahi lagne wala number banata hai, jaisa Chapter 2 ne bataya. Meeting aksar fine-tuning suggest karegi, kyunki “model ko hamari policies sikhao” sahi lagta hai. Lekin fine-tune kiye model ko har baar number badalne par dobara train karna padta hai, aur woh ab bhi user ko nahi dikha sakta ki 45 kahan se aaya.',
  'This is one of the most common misdiagnoses in the field, and it is expensive because the wrong answer sounds reasonable.':
    'Yeh field ki sabse aam galat diagnoses mein se ek hai, aur mehngi hai kyunki galat jawab samajhdaar lagta hai.',
  'Diagnose the kind of failure':
    'Failure ki kism ki jaanch kijiye',
  'So ask “what kind of failure is this?” before you ask “which fix?”. There are four kinds, and each points to its own fix:':
    'Isliye “kaunsa fix?” poochhne se pehle “yeh kis kism ka failure hai?” poochhiye. Chaar kismein hain, aur har ek apne fix ki taraf ishaara karti hai:',
  '<strong>It does not know.</strong> The answer is missing, out of date or invented. → Improve the evidence, and version your documents (Chapter 12).':
    '<strong>Ise pata nahi.</strong> Jawab missing, purana ya banaaya hua hai. → Saboot sudhaariye, aur apne documents ka version rakhiye (Chapter 12).',
  '<strong>It knows, but behaves wrongly.</strong> The content is right but the format, tone or rule-following is wrong. → Improve the instructions first, then require a format (Chapter 8), and fine-tune only if those stop helping.':
    '<strong>Ise pata hai, lekin galat behave karta hai.</strong> Content sahi hai lekin format, tone ya niyam maanna galat hai. → Pehle instructions sudhaariye, phir format zaroori kijiye (Chapter 8), aur fine-tune tabhi kijiye jab yeh madad karna band kar dein.',
  '<strong>It cannot work it out.</strong> Several steps of logic, dependent calculations or real ambiguity. → Use reasoning or a stronger model (Chapter 11).':
    '<strong>Yeh hisaab nahi laga paata.</strong> Logic ke kai steps, aapas mein jude calculations ya asli ambiguity. → Reasoning ya mazboot model use kijiye (Chapter 11).',
  '<strong>It is right but too expensive.</strong> Too slow or too costly at your volume. → Use a smaller model, or a cheap-first cascade (Chapter 15).':
    '<strong>Yeh sahi hai lekin bahut mehnga.</strong> Aapke volume par bahut dheema ya mehnga. → Chhota model, ya sasta-pehle cascade use kijiye (Chapter 15).',
  'Next to each failure, write one letter: <strong>K</strong> (does not know), <strong>B</strong> (behaves wrongly), <strong>R</strong> (cannot work it out) or <strong>E</strong> (too expensive). Choose a single letter even when it is hard; the hard ones teach you the most.':
    'Har failure ke bagal mein ek akshar likhiye: <strong>K</strong> (pata nahi), <strong>B</strong> (galat behave karta hai), <strong>R</strong> (hisaab nahi laga paata) ya <strong>E</strong> (bahut mehnga). Mushkil ho tab bhi ek hi akshar chuniye; mushkil wale sabse zyada sikhaate hain.',
  'The result is usually uneven. Most real failure lists are dominated by K and B. That is why better retrieval and prompting produce most of the improvement in most products, and why fine-tuning proposals often fail to deliver.':
    'Nateeja aam taur par asamaan hota hai. Zyadatar asli failure lists mein K aur B haavi hote hain. Isiliye zyadatar products mein behtar retrieval aur prompting zyadatar sudhaar laate hain, aur fine-tuning prastaav aksar vaada poora nahi karte.',
  'Fine-tuning teaches behaviour, not facts. If the complaint is “it does not know our policy”, fine-tuning is the wrong tool.':
    'Fine-tuning behaviour sikhaata hai, facts nahi. Agar shikaayat “ise hamari policy nahi pata” hai, to fine-tuning galat tool hai.',
  'This diagnosis needs a named failure with a count behind it: your Chapter 14.5 list. Without one, the discussion becomes a contest of opinions, and the most senior opinion usually wins.':
    'Is diagnosis ko ek naam wala failure chahiye jiske peechhe ginti ho: aapki Chapter 14.5 list. Iske bina charcha raayon ki ladaai ban jaati hai, aur aam taur par sabse senior raay jeet-ti hai.',
  'Diagnose a real failure you have seen in an AI feature, yours or one you use. Write what the user saw, which of the four kinds it is, and the fix. Then write the one measurement that would show you chose correctly.':
    'Kisi AI feature mein dekhe ek asli failure ki jaanch kijiye, aapka ya jise aap use karte hain. Likhiye ki user ne kya dekha, yeh chaar mein se kaunsi kism hai, aur fix kya hai. Phir woh ek measurement likhiye jo dikhaye ki aapne sahi chuna.',
  'the user saw … kind of failure … the fix … I would know I was right if …':
    'user ne dekha … failure ki kism … fix … mujhe pata chalega ki main sahi tha agar …',
  'Classifying is the hard part, because failures often look alike. “It gave a confident wrong figure” could be any of the four until you check what was retrieved. If the right passage was retrieved and misread, it is behaviour or reasoning. If the wrong passage was retrieved, only better retrieval helps. If the right passage is not in the documents at all, the fix comes before anything in this course. The measurement matters too: “the right passage is retrieved 9 times in 10 instead of 6” can be checked; “it feels better” cannot.':
    'Classify karna mushkil hissa hai, kyunki failures aksar ek jaise dikhte hain. “Isne confident galat figure diya” chaaron mein se koi bhi ho sakta hai jab tak aap check na karein ki kya retrieve hua. Agar sahi passage retrieve hua aur galat padha gaya, to behaviour ya reasoning hai. Agar galat passage retrieve hua, to sirf behtar retrieval madad karta hai. Agar sahi passage documents mein hai hi nahi, to fix is course ki har cheez se pehle aata hai. Measurement bhi maayne rakhta hai: “sahi passage 6 ki jagah 10 mein 9 baar retrieve hota hai” check ho sakta hai; “behtar lagta hai” nahi.',
  'What fine-tuning really costs':
    'Fine-tuning ki asli keemat kya hai',
  'Fine-tuning does provide real benefits. It gives <strong>consistency</strong>: the same structure and tone across thousands of outputs, more reliably than instructions. It lets a <strong>small model do a narrow job</strong> about as well as a large one, which saves a lot of money. And it teaches conventions that are hard to describe but easy to show, such as house style.':
    'Fine-tuning asli fayde deta hai. Yeh <strong>consistency</strong> deta hai: hazaaron outputs mein wahi structure aur tone, instructions se zyada bharose se. Yeh <strong>chhote model ko ek sankara kaam</strong> lagbhag bade jitna achha karne deta hai, jisse kaafi paise bachte hain. Aur yeh woh tareeke sikhaata hai jinhe describe karna mushkil par dikhana aasaan hai, jaise house style.',
  'It also has costs that proposals leave out. Someone must create the training examples and <em>keep them up to date</em>. You need a test set in advance, or you cannot tell whether it helped. You must retrain every time the base model is retired, as in Chapter 18. And your improvement now lives inside one provider’s system instead of in your prompt and your index.':
    'Iski aisi costs bhi hain jo prastaav chhod dete hain. Kisi ko training examples banaane aur <em>unhe update rakhne</em> padte hain. Aapko pehle se test set chahiye, warna aap nahi bata sakte ki madad mili. Har baar base model retire hone par dobara train karna padta hai, jaise Chapter 18 mein. Aur aapka sudhaar ab aapke prompt aur index ki jagah ek provider ke system ke andar rehta hai.',
  'Cost a fine-tuning proposal':
    'Fine-tuning prastaav ki cost nikaaliye',
  'Take the most likely fine-tuning candidate from your list and write the full cost, not just the training bill. How many labelled examples? Who writes them? Who maintains them when the product changes? What test proves it worked? And what happens to all of it when the base model is retired in eighteen months?':
    'Apni list ka sabse sambhavit fine-tuning ummeedwaar lijiye aur poori cost likhiye, sirf training ka bill nahi. Kitne labelled examples? Unhe kaun likhta hai? Product badalne par unhe kaun sambhaalta hai? Kaunsa test prove karta hai ki yeh kaam kiya? Aur atharah mahine mein base model retire hone par iska kya hota hai?',
  'The total is several times the number on the vendor’s pricing page. You also get a list of owners. A fine-tuning proposal with no named owner for the training data will decay.':
    'Kul vendor ke pricing page ke number ka kai guna hota hai. Aapko owners ki list bhi milti hai. Jis fine-tuning prastaav mein training data ka koi naam wala owner nahi, woh sad jaayega.',
  'Try a smaller model':
    'Chhota model try kijiye',
  'The option teams test least is often the one with the biggest effect: <strong>going smaller</strong>. A cheaper, faster model, sometimes trained to imitate a larger one on your task, often decides the economics of a high-volume feature. Narrow, repetitive, high-volume, time-sensitive tasks are where small models do well.':
    'Jo vikalp teams sabse kam test karti hain woh aksar sabse zyada asar wala hota hai: <strong>chhota hona</strong>. Sasta, tez model, kabhi aapke task par bade ki nakal karne ke liye train kiya hua, aksar high-volume feature ki arthvyavastha tay karta hai. Sankare, dohraaye jaane wale, high-volume, samay-sanvedansheel tasks mein chhote models achha karte hain.',
  'Estimate the saving from a smaller model':
    'Chhote model se bachat ka andaaza lagaiye',
  'Pick the narrowest, highest-volume task in your product, such as routing, classification, extraction or a short summary. Estimate its share of total query volume. Then use the cost model below to work out what it would cost on a model one or two tiers cheaper.':
    'Apne product ka sabse sankara, sabse zyada volume wala task chuniye, jaise routing, classification, extraction ya chhota summary. Kul query volume mein uske hisse ka andaaza lagaiye. Phir neeche ke cost model se nikaaliye ki ek-do tier saste model par iski cost kya hogi.',
  'This is often the largest single saving available, in the least exciting part of the product. Most teams never test it.':
    'Yeh aksar sabse badi akeli bachat hoti hai, product ke sabse kam romaanchak hisse mein. Zyadatar teams ise kabhi test nahi karti.',
  'Work in this order: instructions, then evidence, then fine-tuning, then a different model, measuring after each. The first two can be undone in hours, so ruling them out is cheap. Fine-tuning commits you to maintenance for as long as the feature exists.':
    'Is kram mein kaam kijiye: instructions, phir saboot, phir fine-tuning, phir alag model, har ek ke baad naapte hue. Pehle do ghanton mein palte ja sakte hain, isliye unhe khaarij karna sasta hai. Fine-tuning aapko tab tak maintenance se baandh deta hai jab tak feature maujood hai.',
  'You cannot see the effect of any of the four changes without a test set. A team with an answer key can settle “should we fine-tune?” in a week. A team without one cannot settle it at all.':
    'Test set ke bina aap chaaron mein se kisi badlaav ka asar nahi dekh sakte. Answer key wali team “kya fine-tune karein?” ek hafte mein tay kar sakti hai. Jiske paas nahi, woh ise tay hi nahi kar sakti.',
  'Designing for wrong answers: evidence, confidence and refusals':
    'Galat jawabon ke liye design: saboot, confidence aur refusals',
  'At 90% accuracy, one answer in ten is wrong. Whether the feature is usable depends on what the screen does about that one. You will audit a real product, design four interface states, time a correction and design the refusal.':
    '90% accuracy par das mein ek jawab galat hota hai. Feature use laayak hai ya nahi, yeh is par nirbhar hai ki screen us ek ke saath kya karti hai. Aap ek asli product ka audit karenge, chaar interface states design karenge, ek correction ka samay naapenge aur refusal design karenge.',
  'Explain how a feature that is wrong one time in ten can still be trusted.':
    'Samjhaana ki das mein ek baar galat hone wale feature par bhi bharosa kaise ho sakta hai.',
  'Say what to do with a confidence score, and why displaying it as a number is usually wrong.':
    'Batana ki confidence score ka kya karna hai, aur use number ki tarah dikhana aam taur par galat kyun hai.',
  'Explain what must exist underneath a kill switch for it to be usable.':
    'Samjhaana ki kill switch use laayak hone ke liye uske neeche kya hona chahiye.',
  'Design the four states for a real feature':
    'Ek asli feature ke liye chaar states design kijiye',
  'Many AI features use one interface for four different situations, so a confident wrong answer looks exactly like a confident right one. Design the states properly for a real feature, and time how long a correction takes.':
    'Kai AI features chaar alag situations ke liye ek hi interface use karte hain, isliye confident galat jawab bilkul confident sahi jawab jaisa dikhta hai. Ek asli feature ke liye states theek se design kijiye, aur naapiye ki correction mein kitna samay lagta hai.',
  'Audit an AI feature you use every day. Note what it shows when it is confident, unsure, wrong and unable to answer.':
    'Roz use kiye kisi AI feature ka audit kijiye. Note kijiye ki woh confident, anishchit, galat aur jawab na de paane par kya dikhata hai.',
  'Pick a feature you own or could own. Write the four states: what the user sees, and what they can do next, in each.':
    'Apna ya ho sakne wala ek feature chuniye. Chaar states likhiye: har ek mein user kya dekhta hai, aur aage kya kar sakta hai.',
  'Decide what the interface shows when confidence is middling, so uncertainty is visible without being noisy.':
    'Tay kijiye ki beech ke confidence par interface kya dikhata hai, taaki anishchitata shor mache bina dikhe.',
  'Time the correction: from a user noticing a mistake to it being fixed. Count every step and hand-off.':
    'Correction ka samay naapiye: user ke galti notice karne se theek hone tak. Har step aur hand-off giniye.',
  'Write down which of the four states your current design merges, and what that costs the user.':
    'Likhiye ki aapka current design chaar mein se kaunse states mila deta hai, aur user ko iski kya keemat padti hai.',
  'The correction path is timed end to end, and the slowest step is identified.':
    'Correction ka raasta shuru se ant tak time kiya gaya hai, aur sabse dheema step pehchaana gaya hai.',
  'You can name the state your product handles worst, and what you would change first.':
    'Aap woh state bata sakte hain jise aapka product sabse bura sambhalta hai, aur aap pehle kya badlenge.',
  'A required quote makes checking cheap':
    'Zaroori quote check karna sasta banata hai',
  'A quote is more useful than a confidence number.':
    'Quote confidence number se zyada kaam ka hai.',
  'Users notice the slow responses':
    'Users dheeme responses notice karte hain',
  'Rolling back code does not undo behaviour both versions share.':
    'Code rollback karna woh behaviour nahi palatta jo dono versions mein hai.',
  'No code. Pick an AI feature you use every day, and one feature you own or could own.':
    'Koi code nahi. Roz use kiya ek AI feature chuniye, aur ek feature jo aapka hai ya ho sakta hai.',
  'So far the course has focused on making the model right more often. This chapter is about the rest of the time. At 90% accuracy, one interaction in ten is wrong, and no amount of engineering removes that entirely. What the screen does in that case decides whether the feature is usable.':
    'Ab tak course ne model ko zyada baar sahi banaane par dhyaan diya. Yeh chapter baaki samay ke baare mein hai. 90% accuracy par das mein ek interaction galat hota hai, aur koi engineering ise poori tarah nahi hataati. Us case mein screen kya karti hai, yahi tay karta hai ki feature use laayak hai ya nahi.',
  'This is a design decision, and it belongs to the product owner. An engineer can tell you a confidence score exists. The product owner decides what the user sees when it is low.':
    'Yeh design decision hai, aur product owner ka hai. Engineer bata sakta hai ki confidence score maujood hai. Product owner tay karta hai ki kam hone par user kya dekhta hai.',
  'Do not show an uncertain answer in a confident interface. Many AI features feel untrustworthy because they show a wrong answer exactly the way they show a right one, not because they are less accurate.':
    'Anishchit jawab ko confident interface mein mat dikhaiye. Kai AI features par bharosa isliye nahi hota kyunki woh galat jawab bilkul sahi jawab ki tarah dikhate hain, isliye nahi ki woh kam accurate hain.',
  'There are four things to get right. A feature that does all four can be wrong one time in ten and still be trusted. One that does none will be distrusted even at 95% accuracy.':
    'Chaar cheezein sahi karni hain. Chaaron karne wala feature das mein ek baar galat hokar bhi bharose laayak ho sakta hai. Koi na karne wale par 95% accuracy par bhi bharosa nahi hoga.',
  '1. Show the evidence':
    '1. Saboot dikhaiye',
  'A link that opens the actual source passage lets a user check a claim in seconds. That is why Chapter 8 required the model to quote its source. A citation that names a document but does not open it is worse than nothing: it looks checkable, but the user cannot check it, and cannot tell until it matters.':
    'Asli source passage kholne wala link user ko seconds mein claim check karne deta hai. Isiliye Chapter 8 ne model se source quote karwaaya. Jo citation document ka naam le lekin use khole nahi woh kuchh na hone se bhi bura hai: woh check karne laayak lagta hai, lekin user check nahi kar sakta, aur tab tak pata nahi chalta jab tak zaroorat na pade.',
  'Audit an AI feature you use every day':
    'Roz use kiye AI feature ka audit kijiye',
  'Pick one, such as a search assistant, an email drafter or a coding assistant. Ask it something it will get wrong, at the edge of what it knows.':
    'Ek chuniye, jaise search assistant, email drafter ya coding assistant. Usse kuchh aisa poochhiye jo woh galat karega, uski jaankari ke kinaare par.',
  'Then answer four questions in writing. Could you check the claim, and how many seconds did it take? Did the interface show the wrong answer any differently from a right one? What could you do about it? And what happened to your correction?':
    'Phir chaar sawaalon ke likhit jawab dijiye. Kya aap claim check kar paaye, aur kitne second lage? Kya interface ne galat jawab ko sahi se kisi bhi tarah alag dikhaya? Aap uske baare mein kya kar sakte the? Aur aapke correction ka kya hua?',
  'Most well-known products fail at least two of the four. Note which ones. Users will hold your feature to the same standard.':
    'Zyadatar mashhoor products chaar mein se kam se kam do mein fail hote hain. Note kijiye kaunse. Users aapke feature ko isi maanak par parkhenge.',
  '2. Design for speed':
    '2. Speed ke liye design kijiye',
  'Chapter 11 treated slow responses as a cost. Here they are a design problem. Streaming works for prose, because a partly arrived paragraph is already useful. It does not work for everything. A number that appears and then changes as generation continues is worse than a spinner. The user has already read it and may have acted on it.':
    'Chapter 11 ne dheeme responses ko cost maana. Yahan woh design problem hain. Streaming prose ke liye kaam karti hai, kyunki aadha aaya paragraph bhi kaam ka hai. Yeh har cheez ke liye kaam nahi karti. Jo number dikhe aur phir generation ke saath badle woh spinner se bhi bura hai. User use pehle hi padh chuka hai aur shayad us par kaam bhi kar chuka.',
  '3. Use confidence to choose behaviour':
    '3. Behaviour chunne ke liye confidence use kijiye',
  'Predict: your model returns a confidence score with every answer. What should the interface do with it?':
    'Andaaza lagaiye: aapka model har jawab ke saath confidence score lautata hai. Interface ko iska kya karna chahiye?',
  'Use it to decide what the product does, and do not display it as a number. A percentage next to an answer asks the user to judge something they cannot calibrate, and the model’s own confidence is often badly calibrated anyway. Used internally, it can change the behaviour: answer directly, show the evidence first, ask a clarifying question, or pass the case to a person.':
    'Ise product kya kare yeh tay karne ke liye use kijiye, aur number ki tarah mat dikhaiye. Jawab ke bagal ka percentage user se aisi cheez parakhne ko kehta hai jise woh calibrate nahi kar sakta, aur model ka apna confidence aksar waise bhi theek se calibrated nahi hota. Andar use karne par yeh behaviour badal sakta hai: seedha jawab dena, pehle saboot dikhana, ek spasht karne wala sawaal poochhna, ya case insaan ko dena.',
  'Turn confidence into interface choices: an editable field instead of a fixed one, a draft instead of a sent message, or a question instead of a guess.':
    'Confidence ko interface choices mein badliye: fixed ki jagah editable field, bheje message ki jagah draft, ya andaaze ki jagah sawaal.',
  'For one feature you own, write what the user sees in four states: a confident answer, a low-confidence answer, a refusal, and the AI turned off. Write the actual screen content.':
    'Apne ek feature ke liye likhiye ki user chaar states mein kya dekhta hai: confident jawab, kam-confidence jawab, refusal, aur AI band. Screen ka asli content likhiye.',
  'The third and fourth states are the hard ones, and most specs leave them out. If you cannot write them, the product does not have them either; it just does whatever the code happens to do.':
    'Teesra aur chautha state mushkil hain, aur zyadatar specs unhe chhod dete hain. Agar aap unhe nahi likh sakte, to product mein bhi nahi hain; woh bas wahi karta hai jo code karta ho.',
  '4. Make correcting it easy':
    '4. Correct karna aasaan banaiye',
  'When the system is wrong, what the user does next is your most valuable data, and most products throw it away. A thumbs-down records that something was wrong, but not what.':
    'Jab system galat hota hai, to user aage jo karta hai woh aapka sabse keemti data hai, aur zyadatar products use phenk dete hain. Thumbs-down record karta hai ki kuchh galat tha, yeh nahi ki kya.',
  'A good correction path captures what the user expected <em>instead</em>, keeps the evidence the system used, and is faster than giving up and doing the task by hand. If correcting takes longer than the manual workaround, nobody corrects, and an empty feedback table looks like satisfaction.':
    'Achha correction raasta capture karta hai ki user ko <em>iski jagah</em> kya chahiye tha, system ka use kiya saboot rakhta hai, aur haar kar kaam haath se karne se tez hota hai. Agar correct karna manual tareeke se zyada samay le, to koi correct nahi karta, aur khaali feedback table santushti jaisi lagti hai.',
  'Time a correction':
    'Correction ka samay naapiye',
  'Use a clock. How long does it take to correct a wrong output, compared with doing the task by hand from scratch? Do it three times.':
    'Ghadi use kijiye. Galat output ko correct karne mein kitna samay lagta hai, kaam ko shuru se haath se karne ke muqaable? Teen baar kijiye.',
  'If correcting is slower, your feedback table will stay empty, and you may wrongly read that as satisfaction. This one measurement explains most “our users never give feedback” complaints.':
    'Agar correct karna dheema hai, to aapki feedback table khaali rahegi, aur aap use galti se santushti samajh sakte hain. Yeh ek measurement “hamare users kabhi feedback nahi dete” wali zyadatar shikaayaton ko samjhaata hai.',
  'Example':
    'Example',
  'Two products use the same model and the same retrieval. One logs a thumbs-down. The other logs the answer, the retrieved chunks and the question. It also asks one thing: “what did you expect instead?” Within two weeks, the second has a list of real failure types and a roadmap built from its own traffic. The first has a falling number and no idea why.':
    'Do products ek hi model aur ek hi retrieval use karte hain. Ek thumbs-down log karta hai. Doosra jawab, retrieve kiye chunks aur sawaal log karta hai. Woh ek cheez aur poochhta hai: “aapko iski jagah kya chahiye tha?” Do hafte mein doosre ke paas asli failure types ki list aur apne traffic se bana roadmap hota hai. Pehle ke paas girta number hai aur koi andaaza nahi kyun.',
  'Design the correction path for a feature you know. What does the user do when the output is wrong, what does that action record, and how long does it take compared with doing the task by hand? Then write the test case it would produce.':
    'Kisi jaane-pehchaane feature ka correction raasta design kijiye. Output galat hone par user kya karta hai, woh action kya record karta hai, aur kaam haath se karne ke muqaable kitna samay lagta hai? Phir woh test case likhiye jo isse banega.',
  'A good design makes correcting the fastest option. Let the user edit the output in place, and treat the edit as the feedback. They were going to fix it anyway, so it costs them nothing, and you learn the expected answer exactly. Record the question, the evidence, the output and the correction together. Without the evidence, you know the answer was wrong but not whether retrieval or generation caused it, which is the distinction Chapter 19 needs.':
    'Achha design correct karne ko sabse tez vikalp banata hai. User ko output wahin edit karne dijiye, aur edit ko hi feedback maaniye. Woh waise bhi theek karne wale the, isliye unhe kuchh nahi padta, aur aapko ummeed ka jawab bilkul sahi pata chalta hai. Sawaal, saboot, output aur correction saath record kijiye. Saboot ke bina aapko pata hai ki jawab galat tha, lekin yeh nahi ki retrieval ne ya generation ne kiya, aur yahi farq Chapter 19 ko chahiye.',
  'Design the refusal':
    'Refusal design kijiye',
  'Every system looks good when it works. Trust is built on the screen that says <em>I do not have that</em>, and many AI products design that screen last or not at all.':
    'Har system kaam karte samay achha dikhta hai. Bharosa us screen par banta hai jo kehti hai <em>mere paas yeh nahi hai</em>, aur kai AI products us screen ko aakhir mein ya bilkul design nahi karte.',
  'A system that says “I cannot answer this” and offers a route to a person earns more trust than one that always produces something. Users judge a system partly by its refusals. A feature that never refuses teaches them that its confidence means nothing.':
    'Jo system kehta hai “main iska jawab nahi de sakta” aur insaan tak raasta deta hai, woh hamesha kuchh na kuchh dene wale se zyada bharosa kamaata hai. Users system ko kuchh had tak uske refusals se parakhte hain. Kabhi mana na karne wala feature unhe sikhaata hai ki uske confidence ka koi matlab nahi.',
  'What happens when the AI is off':
    'AI band hone par kya hota hai',
  'Finally, decide what the feature does when the AI is switched off. Chapter 18 separated a rollback from a kill switch. A kill switch is only usable if there is something underneath it: search without generated answers, a form without extraction, or a queue without routing. If turning the AI off leaves a blank screen, the switch just replaces one failure with another.':
    'Aakhir mein tay kijiye ki AI band hone par feature kya karta hai. Chapter 18 ne rollback ko kill switch se alag kiya. Kill switch tabhi use laayak hai jab uske neeche kuchh ho: bina generate jawab ka search, bina extraction ka form, ya bina routing ki queue. Agar AI band karne se khaali screen reh jaaye, to switch bas ek failure ko doosre se badal deta hai.',
  'Measuring business impact: designing a pilot':
    'Business impact naapna: pilot design karna',
  'A system can be accurate and still change nothing for the business. You will find the slow part of the workflow, then design a pilot with a business metric, a comparison, a failure threshold and a time window.':
    'System accurate hokar bhi business ke liye kuchh na badle, aisa ho sakta hai. Aap workflow ka dheema hissa dhoondhenge, phir business metric, tulna, failure threshold aur time window ke saath ek pilot design karenge.',
  'Explain why a system that measures well can still produce no business benefit.':
    'Samjhaana ki achha naapne wala system bhi business fayda kyun nahi de sakta.',
  'Design a pilot that could fail':
    'Aisa pilot design kijiye jo fail ho sake',
  'Design a pilot for a real feature, with a number the business already tracks, a comparison, a failure threshold and a time window. Then get someone senior to agree the threshold before it runs.':
    'Ek asli feature ke liye pilot design kijiye, us number ke saath jo business pehle se track karta hai, ek tulna, ek failure threshold aur time window. Phir chalne se pehle kisi senior se threshold par sehmati lijiye.',
  'Time the whole workflow and mark where your feature fits. If it is not on the critical path, say so and stop here.':
    'Poore workflow ka samay naapiye aur mark kijiye ki aapka feature kahan fit hota hai. Agar yeh critical path par nahi, to yahi kahiye aur yahin rukiye.',
  'Choose the business number. It must already exist, and someone must already look at it.':
    'Business number chuniye. Yeh pehle se maujood hona chahiye, aur koi pehle se use dekhta ho.',
  'Design the comparison: which two groups, over which period, and why they are comparable.':
    'Tulna design kijiye: kaunse do groups, kis avadhi mein, aur woh tulniya kyun hain.',
  'Write the failure threshold, the change below which you would call it a failure, and the time window before you judge.':
    'Failure threshold likhiye, woh badlaav jiske neeche aap ise failure kahenge, aur faisle se pehle ki time window.',
  'Write the disappointing result in advance, in the words you would say to whoever funded it.':
    'Nirasha wala result pehle hi likhiye, un shabdon mein jo aap funding dene wale se kahenge.',
  'Get the person who funds it to agree the threshold in writing <em>before</em> the pilot runs.':
    'Funding dene wale se pilot chalne se <em>pehle</em> threshold par likhit sehmati lijiye.',
  'The number is one the business was already tracking before the pilot.':
    'Number woh hai jise business pilot se pehle track kar raha tha.',
  'The failure threshold is agreed in writing by the person who would be disappointed by it.':
    'Failure threshold par us insaan ki likhit sehmati hai jo usse niraash hoga.',
  'You can describe a result that would make you recommend switching the feature off.':
    'Aap aisa result bata sakte hain jo aapse feature band karne ki salaah dilwaaye.',
  'Recall, precision, judges and per-category scores.':
    'Recall, precision, judges aur per-category scores.',
  'No code. Bring a feature you have measured, yours or one from the course, and the name of whoever pays for it.':
    'Koi code nahi. Apna ya course ka ek naapa hua feature laaiye, aur uske liye paise dene wale ka naam.',
  'So far the course has measured the system: whether retrieval is right, whether the judge can be trusted, whether the classifier is accurate per category. All of that is necessary. None of it answers the question that decides future funding: did it help the business?':
    'Ab tak course ne system naapa: retrieval sahi hai ya nahi, judge par bharosa ho sakta hai ya nahi, classifier har category mein accurate hai ya nahi. Yeh sab zaroori hai. In mein se koi bhi us sawaal ka jawab nahi deta jo aage ki funding tay karta hai: kya isne business ki madad ki?',
  'A system can be 94% accurate and change nothing, because nobody uses it, or because the step it speeds up was never the slow part.':
    'System 94% accurate hokar bhi kuchh na badle, kyunki koi use nahi karta, ya kyunki jo step yeh tez karta hai woh kabhi dheema tha hi nahi.',
  'Find the slow part first':
    'Pehle dheema hissa dhoondhiye',
  'Time the whole workflow':
    'Poore workflow ka samay naapiye',
  'Take the workflow your feature is part of and time it honestly from start to finish. Include every step, including time spent waiting for other people.':
    'Jis workflow ka aapka feature hissa hai use lijiye aur shuru se ant tak imaandaari se samay naapiye. Har step shaamil kijiye, doosre logon ke intezaar ka samay bhi.',
  'The AI step is rarely the largest. Often the biggest block is waiting for a person, or a handover between two systems. Turning a four-minute step into a one-minute step inside a three-day process will not be noticed.':
    'AI step shayad hi sabse bada hota hai. Aksar sabse bada hissa kisi insaan ka intezaar, ya do systems ke beech hand-over hota hai. Teen din ki process mein chaar minute ke step ko ek minute karna kisi ko nahi dikhega.',
  'This is the cheapest study in the course and the one most often skipped, because it can show that you should not build the feature.':
    'Yeh course ka sabse sasta adhyayan hai aur sabse zyada chhoota hua, kyunki yeh dikha sakta hai ki aapko feature banaana hi nahi chahiye.',
  'Four parts of a pilot':
    'Pilot ke chaar hisse',
  'If the step you are speeding up really is on the critical path, you can design a pilot. Treat a pilot as a test that states in advance what result would disappoint you, rather than as a small launch.':
    'Agar aap jo step tez kar rahe hain woh sach mein critical path par hai, to aap pilot design kar sakte hain. Pilot ko chhote launch ki jagah aise test ki tarah dekhiye jo pehle se batata hai ki kaunsa result aapko niraash karega.',
  '<strong>The number.</strong> One measure the business already tracks, such as handling time, first-contact resolution, backlog age or error rate. Do not invent a new metric for the pilot.':
    '<strong>Number.</strong> Ek maap jo business pehle se track karta hai, jaise handling time, first-contact resolution, backlog age ya error rate. Pilot ke liye naya metric mat banaiye.',
  '<strong>The comparison.</strong> The same team before and after is weak evidence. Two comparable groups over the same period is much stronger, and usually possible.':
    '<strong>Tulna.</strong> Ek hi team pehle aur baad kamzor saboot hai. Ek hi avadhi mein do tulniya groups kahin mazboot hain, aur aam taur par sambhav.',
  '<strong>The failure threshold.</strong> The change below which you will call it a failure, written down before you start.':
    '<strong>Failure threshold.</strong> Woh badlaav jiske neeche aap ise failure kahenge, shuru karne se pehle likha hua.',
  '<strong>The time window.</strong> Long enough for the novelty to wear off. The first two weeks with any new tool make it look better than it is.':
    '<strong>Time window.</strong> Itni lambi ki naya-pan utar jaaye. Kisi bhi naye tool ke pehle do hafte use asal se behtar dikhate hain.',
  'Before running anything, write the sentence you would have to say if the pilot showed no effect. Use the words you would say to the person who funded it.':
    'Kuchh bhi chalaane se pehle woh sentence likhiye jo pilot ka koi asar na hone par aapko kehna padega. Woh shabd use kijiye jo aap funding dene wale se kahenge.',
  'This shows two things. Whether you actually have a failure threshold; many pilots do not. And whether the pilot could ever produce that sentence, or whether every outcome would be reported as success.':
    'Isse do baatein dikhti hain. Kya aapke paas sach mein failure threshold hai; kai pilots ke paas nahi hota. Aur kya pilot kabhi woh sentence de sakta tha, ya har nateeja success hi bataya jaata.',
  'If a pilot cannot fail, it is really a launch.':
    'Agar pilot fail nahi ho sakta, to woh asal mein launch hai.',
  'When the system works but the number does not move':
    'Jab system kaam kare lekin number na hile',
  'Your pilot shows the system works well, but the business number does not move. Write the three explanations you would investigate first, in order.':
    'Aapka pilot dikhata hai ki system achha kaam karta hai, lekin business number nahi hilta. Woh teen vyakhyaayein likhiye jinki aap pehle jaanch karenge, kram mein.',
  'This order usually works best. First, are people using it? Low adoption is the most common cause and the easiest to check. Second, does the output reach the place where the decision is made, or is it in a separate tool someone has to remember to open? Third, was the step you sped up actually on the critical path? Only after these three should you question system quality, even though teams usually check it first because they know how to measure it.':
    'Yeh kram aam taur par sabse achha kaam karta hai. Pehla, kya log ise use kar rahe hain? Kam adoption sabse aam kaaran hai aur check karna sabse aasaan. Doosra, kya output wahan pahunchta hai jahan faisla hota hai, ya ek alag tool mein jise kholna yaad rakhna padta hai? Teesra, kya aapka tez kiya step sach mein critical path par tha? In teeno ke baad hi system quality par sawaal uthaaiye, jabki teams aam taur par use pehle check karti hain kyunki woh use naapna jaanti hain.',
  'The whole course repeats one idea at larger and larger scale: decide what counts as failure, then measure that specific thing, instead of looking at outputs and forming an impression. You have done it for a prompt, a retriever, a judge, a cost model and now a business case.':
    'Poora course ek hi idea ko badhte paimaane par dohrata hai: tay kijiye ki failure kya hai, phir outputs dekh kar raay banaane ki jagah usi specific cheez ko naapiye. Aapne yeh ek prompt, ek retriever, ek judge, ek cost model aur ab ek business case ke liye kiya.',
  'The techniques will change as models change. The habit of defining failure first and then measuring it is what carries over.':
    'Models badalne ke saath techniques badlengi. Pehle failure tay karne aur phir use naapne ki aadat aage kaam aati hai.'

});
